Refuse httpd path components ending in a dot or space on Windows.
Windows drops dots and spaces from the end of a file or directory name,
so "httpd.conf." and "httpd.conf " open httpd.conf and "adm./" is the
directory adm. The checks on the request path compare names exactly,
so /httpd.conf. sent the configuration file with its passwords,
/adm./secret.htm skipped the password for /adm, and /cgi-bin./x.cgi
sent the source of the program.

No file that httpd can serve has such a name, so refuse any component
that ends in a dot or space once the path is cleaned. This also covers
"..." and ".. ", which are not removed as parent references.

---
 networking/httpd.c |    9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

--- a/networking/httpd.c
+++ b/networking/httpd.c
@@ -2761,6 +2761,15 @@
 	 * alternate data stream (httpd.conf::$DATA) */
 	if (strchr(urlcopy, ':'))
 		send_headers_and_exit(HTTP_NOT_FOUND);
+	/* Windows ignores dots and spaces at the end of a path component,
+	 * so it would take "/httpd.conf." as "/httpd.conf" */
+	for (tptr = urlcopy; *tptr; tptr++) {
+		if ((*tptr == '.' || *tptr == ' ')
+		 && (tptr[1] == '/' || tptr[1] == '\0')
+		) {
+			send_headers_and_exit(HTTP_NOT_FOUND);
+		}
+	}
 #endif
 
 	/* Log it */
